Z||000000||mrfixit58||08-24-2000||04:15 PM||||I'm planning on changing out my struts this weekend. My old ones look like stock (135K miles). I have a set of fairly new Monroe struts already mounted/installed in the spring so this will be a un-bolt / re-bolt project. Does anyone have any tricks to help with the alignment so I don't destroy my tires before I make it to the alignment shop? <P>While apart, I've been thinking of changing out the A-arm bushings. Other than the removal and replacement of the bushings, do I need any special tools to remove the A-arm?<P>Thanks,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||08-24-2000||04:24 PM||||I think they are 18 mm bolts hangin on to the A-Arms. Changing them out is as straight forward as you get. Alignment? I have tried everything I could to keep the alignment but it almost seems to change at the molecular level so that you HAVE to get an alignment with your steering wheel all kittywhompus.||||reg||1
